Reasoning ECG Model

Author: Sabia Irfan

ECG_Gemma.py
-------------

ECG-Gemma3: ECG + Text Multi-Modal Model
This module extends the Gemma3 language model with the ability to process ECG signals alongside text.
It integrates a custom ECG tokenizer/encoder, projection layers, and a multi-modal interface, enabling the model to understand and generate text conditioned on ECG features.

ECGConfig class:
- Configuration for ECG-specific components:
    ecg_token_id: Special token ID for ECG input
    embedding_dim: Dimension of quantized ECG embeddings
    num_quantizers: Number of quantization codebooks    
    codebook_size: Size of each quantizer codebook  
    hidden_size: Hidden state size for ECG projection   
    Inherits from PretrainedConfig (Hugging Face)

ECG_Gemma_config class:
- Extends Gemma3Config with an embedded ECGConfig.

ECG_Gemma_model class (extends Gemma):
- ECG Tokenizer Wrapper (ECG_Tokenizer_Wrapper) for encoding ECG signals
- Projection layers to align ECG feature space with LLM hidden space
- ECG Feature Pipeline:
    Encode raw ECG signals → embeddings
    Chunk + pool → stable temporal features
    Project into LLM hidden dimension
- Methods:
    get_ecg_features: Extract ECG embeddings from raw signals
    tokenize_ecg: Convert projected ECG features into token indices
    forward: Standard language modeling forward pass
    forward_ecg: Generate text conditioned on ECG signals
    generate_text: Simple greedy decoding loop for text

ECG_Gemma3MultiModalProjector (extends Gemma3MultiModalProjector):
- Adds ECG projection layers
-Normalizes ECG embeddings (RMSNorm)
- Projects them into Gemma3’s hidden dimension for fusion with text/vision


ECG_Gemma3ForConditionalGeneration (extends Gemma3ForConditionalGeneration)
- Full ECG-augmented multimodal LLM:
- Ties together language, vision, and ECG encoders
- Defines forward_ecg() to integrate ECG features into text generation
- Computes loss when labels are provided
- Returns ECG_Gemma3CausalLMOutputWithPast, which includes:
    Loss
    Logits
    Past key values
    Hidden states

ECG_Tokenizer_Wrapper → wraps encoder, quantizer, and decoder for ECG signals

Custom prepare_inputs_for_generation() → allows ECG & multimodal inputs during text generation

token_type_ids_mask_function() → handles masking rules for multimodal attention

ECG_GRPO.py
------------

This repository implements a GRPO reinforcement-learning-based reasoning model for ECG data.

Key features:
- LoRA fine-tuning on a quantized base model.
- 4-bit quantization with bitsandbytes for efficiency.
- Adapter training using cross-entropy.
- GRPO training for reward-driven fine-tuning on reasoning tasks.

Function model_4bit:
- Converts the base model to 4 bits using bitsandbyte
- Creating a new Linear4bit layer with the same config, weights as the original in place of every linear layer 

Training Class:
- The Training class provides a wrapper around model initialization, adapter setup (LoRA), quantization, and optimizer configuration for fine-tuning the causal language model
- Freezes the base model weights and attaches LoRA adapters
- Sets up the optimizer
- Handles device placement
- Stores the tokenizer and reward model for later use in training/evaluation
- Quantizes all linear layers (model_4bit)
- Functions include: Training Adapters, Save Adapter Checkpoint, Generate Initial Reports, GRPO

Training Adapters: This method trains the LoRA adapters
- input ids are a concatenation of ECG signals, text for prompt, labels that are the correct generated report  
- input dataloader batches: 
    input_ids: Tensor of shape (batch_size, seq_len) → tokenized input text
    labels: Tensor of shape (batch_size, seq_len) → tokenized target/output text
    attention_mask (optional): Tensor of shape (batch_size, seq_len) → mask for padding tokens
- Uses CrossEntropyLoss
- Mixed precision: forward/backward passes in autocast(dtype=torch.bfloat16) for faster training and lower memory usage
- Forward Pass: 
    Model outputs logits (batch_size, seq_len, vocab_size)
    Logits and labels are reshaped for CrossEntropyLoss.
- Gradient Accumulation:
    Loss is divided by gradient_accumulation_steps
    Accumulates gradients over multiple steps before performing an optimizer update
-Backward Pass
    Gradients are scaled and backpropagated
    Gradients are clipped (max_norm=1.0) to stabilize training
    Optimizer step & gradient reset occur after accumulation steps
-Logging
    Prints the average loss per epoch for monitoring.

Save Adapter Checkpoint:
- save trained adapter weights at the specified path 

Generate Initial Reports: This method generates text reports using the fine-tuned LoRA adapters
- Load trained adapters
- disables gradients with torch.no_grad() for faster inference
- Generate outputs. Uses model.generate() to produce token sequences
- Converts generated token IDs into text with the tokenizer
- Skips special tokens (like <pad> or <eos>)
- Collects all decoded reports into all_reports and returns 
- Input is input ids and attention mask, no labels or reports, using the rl_dataset 

GRPO: Unfinished RL training - has NOT been adapted to ECG yet 
- Load LoRA adapters from adapter_path into the base model
- Defines tokens that signal the end of a generated response (e.g. "Answer:", "Therefore")
- Epoch Training Loop
    For each epoch:
    Iterate over dataloader batches containing:
        input_ids (prompt text tokens)
        step_answers (reference answers / ground truth steps)
        Attention_mask
        Generate Candidate Outputs
    Use model.generate() with sampling to produce num_candidates outputs per input
- Generation settings:
    do_sample=True, temperature=1.0 → encourages diverse outputs
    max_new_tokens = limit on length of generations
    repetition_penalty=1.2 to reduce repeated phrases   
    stop_token_ids and EOS token to terminate sequences
- Clean + Process Outputs
    Post-process model outputs to align them with reference answers
    Extract numeric answers, filter noise, and detect “thinking” traces
- Reward Calculation:
    Pass cleaned outputs + references into self.reward_model
    Reward model returns scores for each generated candidate
    Compute advantage tensor = candidate score – average score (baseline)
- Log Probability Calculation:
    Tokenize each candidate output
    Run forward pass to compute log probabilities for generated tokens
    Collect log-prob sums for each sequence
- GRPO Loss
    Compute policy gradient–style loss:
    L=−E[log_prob(candidate)×advantage(candidate)]
- Optimization Step
- Backpropagate loss and update adapter weights with optimizer
- Print training progress: epoch, batch number, loss


ECG_Test.py
------------

Prepare Data:
- Load and normalize raw ECG signals (.npy files from MIMIC parquet metadata)
- Load the ECG waveforms as NumPy arrays into a new column ECG_signals

ECG Tokenizer & Model Initialization:
- Loads a pretrained ECG tokenizer model (ECG_Tokenizer_Wrapper) to discretize ECG signals.
- Loads the model checkpoint and applies it to ECG_Gemma_model.
- ECG_Gemma_model integrates ECG features with a generative language model.

ECG Conversion to Torch Tensors:
- Converts each ECG signal to a PyTorch tensor for model input

Tokenizer for LLM (Gemma-7B):
- Adds a special <|ecg|> token to embed ECG sequences into the LLM input.
- Resizes embeddings in the language model to accommodate this new token.

Full Prompt Construction for Supervised Fine-Tuning (SFT):

    full_llm_prompts function:
    - Extract ECG features using model.get_ecg_features.
    - Tokenize ECG features into sequences.
    - Insert ECG tokens into LLM input where <|ecg|> is placed.
    - Pad input IDs and attention masks.
    - Append report tokens for supervised learning.
    - Construct labels tensor: -100 for tokens not in the report (ignored in loss calculation).

    creating_full_prompts function:
    - Iterates over a dataframe of ECG signals + reports.
    - Calls full_llm_prompts for each sample.
    - Returns padded input_ids, attention_mask, and labels for SFT training.

RL Prompt Construction:
    rl_llm_prompts function:
        - Same as full_llm_prompts but excludes labels for RL
    
    rl_prompts function:
    - Converts dataframe to RL-ready input_ids and attention_mask


Collate Functions:

    collate_fn(batch)
    - Pads batches for SFT training.
    - Returns input_ids, attention_mask, and labels.

    rl_collate_fn(batch)
    - Pads batches for RL training.
    - Only returns input_ids and attention_mask.

Dataset Classes:

    TrainingDataset(Dataset):
    - Stores SFT inputs: input_ids, attention_mask, labels.
    - Masks padding tokens in labels to exclude them from loss.

    RLDataset(Dataset):
    - Stores RL-only inputs: input_ids and attention_mask.
    - Casual LLM so no labels included TrainingDataset(Dataset)

Train/Test Split:
- Splits dataset into supervised fine-tuning (SFT) and RL training sets.
- 20 % test size
- Subsamples to speed up experiments.

Convert Tokenized Data to Datasets and DataLoaders:
- Converts tokenized inputs to PyTorch Dataset.
- seperate dataset for RL and SFT
- DataLoaders produce mini-batches for training.

Adapter/LoRA Training Pipeline:
- Initializes LoRA (Low-Rank Adaptation) for parameter-efficient fine-tuning.
- Associates reward model (currently placeholder) for RL training.
- LoRA adapts only selected model layers (q_proj, v_proj) for efficiency.

Insert ECG_Gemma model in Training class and call its functions to train adapters, save weights, generate reports, and GRPO training 